        "original_id": "2c484c6a-2405-5a82-ba45-98b4f1762747",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Marc Rosset, Guillermo Vilas, Renzo Furlan\n- Events: 1992 Olympic Games, 1994 Waldbaum's Hamlet Cup – Singles\n- Topics: Professional tennis, Olympic gold medals, ATP titles, Grand Prix tennis circuit\n\nFacts:\n- Guillermo Vilas was born on 17 August 1952 and is a retired professional tennis player from Argentina.\n- Marc Rosset was born on 7 November 1970 and is a former professional tennis player from Switzerland.\n- Guillermo Vilas finished as the Grand Prix tennis circuit's year-end No. 1 in 1974, 1975, and 1977.\n- Marc Rosset won the men's singles gold medal at the 1992 Olympic Games.\n- In the 1994 Waldbaum's Hamlet Cup – Singles, Marc Rosset was the defending champion but lost in the second round to Renzo Furlan.\n- Guillermo Vilas won four major titles, seven Grand Prix Super Series titles, and 62 ATP titles.",
